# Res Arcana card -> photo rectangle map (consumed by a script that cuts a rough image per card).
# Columns (tab separated): id, name, source, x, y, w, h
#   id     = 0-based position of the card header line (mage|artifact|monument|place|item) in games/res-arcana/data/cards.ra
#   name   = printed German name, exactly as in cards.ra
#   source = photo file name, both live in game-rules/res-arcana/ (not in the repo, copyrighted art)
#   x y w h = pixel rectangle (top-left corner, width, height) of one whole card face in the source photo's own pixels
# Sources: all_cards.jpg (3958x2677, German edition, hand-placed grid of all cards, perspective tilt; the 60 base mages,
#   monuments and artifacts are here, expansion cards are skipped), components.jpg (2911x2572; the 5 places of power
#   and the 8 magic items, which all_cards.jpg does not show).
# Card sizes differ slightly per row because the photo is in perspective, so w and h are per row; rectangles are rough
# (about 5-10 px) and the neighbouring card may graze an edge.
